Now I have a thorough understanding of the project. Let me analyze the 5 failures:

**Failures 1-2 (toggle-all): "element has detached from DOM"**
- When clicking toggle-all, the `render()` function destroys all `<li>` elements via `dom.todoList.innerHTML = ''` and recreates them
- Cypress captures a reference to an `<li>` element, then triggers a click that calls `render()`, which destroys and recreates all `<li>` elements
- The captured reference is now detached from the DOM

**Failures 3-4 (toggle-todo): "element has detached from DOM"**  
- Same root cause: toggling a single todo checkbox triggers `render()` which rebuilds the entire list**Failure 5 (edit-todo, escape): "expected '<li>' to contain 'feed the cat'"**
- The escape key handler correctly resets `editingId = null` and calls `render()`
- BUT the blur handler fires after escape and calls `editTodo(id, e.target.value)` with the current edit input value
- In a real browser, after escape keydown fires, the blur handler fires too, overwriting the original valueLet me look at the escape flow more carefully:

```javascript
dom.todoList.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
  var li = e.target.closest('li');
  if (!li) return;
  var id = parseInt(li.dataset.id, 10);

  if (e.target.classList.contains('edit')) {
    if (e.keyCode === ENTER_KEY) {
      editTodo(id, e.target.value);
      editingId = null;
      render();
    } else if (e.keyCode === ESCAPE_KEY) {
      editingId = null;
      render();
    }
  }
});

dom.todoList.addEventListener('blur', function (e) {
  if (e.target.classList.contains('edit')) {
    var li = e.target.closest('li');
    if (!li) return;
    var id = parseInt(li.dataset.id, 10);
    editTodo(id, e.target.value);
    editingId = null;
    render();
  }
}, true);
```

When escape is pressed, `editingId` gets cleared and `render()` recreates the DOM elements. But then the blur event fires on the original input, triggering `editTodo()` with whatever text was typed, which overwrites the original todo title. The blur handler doesn't check if editing was already cancelled by the escape key.
